  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 143 AM CDT Sat Jun 27 2026\n\nGlobal models indicate a lowering of mid-level heights over our area \nearly to midweek as the upper ridge reorients and builds over the \neastern U.S. This should allow a break from the current heat wave \nwith highs progged to drop back toward normal (low to mid 90s) for \nlate June. Moisture quality improves as the ridge shifts, with \nprecipitable water (PWAT) values climbing toward 1.5\" (near the 75th \npercentile for June). Scattered thunderstorms are expected Monday \nand Tuesday afternoons, particularly over the higher terrain and \nadjacent plains. \n\nThe upper ridge builds back over the area late week bringing a \nreturn to triple digits and drier conditions just in time for the \n4th of July.",
